"text": "The gates below run in order. The harness smoke reads the new backend on this Windows host. - The H2 measurement and its removal are `operator` entries fired in the operator pass: the measurement push, its loop   read, the removal commit, then the final push. - The measurement-only compile check is also `operator`, because after the removal its feature no longer exists. The   wrap never re-runs it. - There is no live leg against a real `claude` this chunk; \"First live test and self-drive\" owns that. - zizmor and the release build run in CI's `lint` / `supply-chain` / `release` jobs and in the pre-push VM stage (the   `pre-push` entry), not as separate local entries. G4 runs in CI's `test` jobs and is read through the final `ci.py`   entry. - `evidence/h2-with-without.md` has no producing entry of its own. It is the recorded result of the operator   loop-log read (the `gh run view <id>` entry), written by the operator pass under the `leg` key's rule that every   operator entry's result is recorded in `evidence/`."
}
